<title>ETHIOPIA: Alitalia resumes flights to Ethiopia.</title>
<headline>Alitalia resumes flights to Ethiopia.</headline>
<dateline>ADDIS ABABA 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian carrier Alitalia has resumed twice-weekly flights between Rome and the Ethiopian capital Addis Ababa after a break of five years, the airline said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Alitalia will fly to Addis Ababa on Tuesdays and Fridays. The first flight took place on June 3.</p>
<p>The national carrier Ethiopian Airlines flies to Rome three times a week. Alitalia began services to Ethiopia in 1965 but discontinued the route in 1992. It offered no explanation at the time.</p>
</text>
